PYTHON CHEAT SHEET  •  Bruce  •  Quick Reference
04
Conditions: if / elif / else
age = 20
if age >= 18:
    print("adult")
elif age >= 13:
    print("teen")
else:
    print("child")
Compound conditions
if age >= 18 and is_citizen:
    print("eligible")
if username == "admin" or is_owner:
    print("access")
if not is_blocked:
    print("continue")
Nested logic
if age >= 18:
    if is_citizen:
        print("eligible")
    else:
        print("citizenship required")
else:
    print("underage")
Boundary checklist
RuleTest values
age >= 1817, 18, 19
score > 9089, 90, 91
price <= 1000999, 1000, 1001
Classic bug:  For an exact condition, do not accidentally write > when the rule says >=. Boundary values are where bugs 
hide like little unemployed goblins.
